ve, adaptive UI across multiple layouts and resolutions. • Strong experience in state management using Redux, Redux Toolkit, Context API, or similar tools. • Experience integrating frontend applications with backend microservices via Web Sockets, REST APIs, Streaming APIs, HTTPS, and g RPC. • Hands-on experience working with microservices architectures and frontendbackend integration patterns. • Strong understanding of React Router and route-based application architecture. • Experience with modern frontend build tooling such as Vite or equivalent. • Robust debugging, profiling, and performance optimization skills for both frontend and backend components. • Familiarity with frontend and backend testing, component validation, and API contract testing. • Proficiency in Git and collaborative development workflows. • Excellent communication and collaboration skills for cross-functional teamwork. Good to Have / Preferred Qualifications • Experience with microfrontend architecture and feature-based frontend organization. • Experience building real-time dashboards, industrial UIs, or visualization-heavy applications. • Experience with waveform, readout, imaging, or graphical rendering interfaces. • Exposure to design token systems, theming, and UI kit integration. • Familiarity with RTK Query, Graph QL abstractions, or structured API abstraction layers. • Experience with error boundaries, offline handling, reconnection logic, connection state management. • Understanding of accessibility, semantic HTML, and enterprise-grade frontend quality practices. • Exposure to Dev Ops / CI-CD pipelines (especially Azure Dev Ops). • Experience in engineering software, industrial software, scientific visualization, healthcare software, or simulation-oriented platforms. • Knowledge of Three.js or &#64;react-three/fiber for advanced visualization use cases. • Familiarity with Vitest, jsdom, or similar frontend testing setups. • Experience with containerization and orchestration (Docker, Kub